{"type":"message","id":"5162ee0c","parentId":"c5fd475d","timestamp":"2026-04-15T10:12:13.694Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have the shared pool progress database: `TeIZbungWasADfsKcnjcogmMnCd`. Let me find its table ID so I can add a new record. Let me check the bitable app first.\n\nActually, I can see the shared pool progress management table is `TeIZbungWasADfsKcnjcogmMnCd`. Let me get its table info.\n\nAlso, the current time is 1744697460000 (2026-04-15 10:11 UTC). The last heartbeat was at 1744686060000 (2026-04-15 06:11 UTC), which is about 4 hours ago (240 minutes), not 60 minutes. But the cron runs every 2 hours (7200 seconds), so 1744686060000 + 7200000 = 1744693260000 which would be 04:41 UTC... Actually let me recalculate.\n\n\nLet me work through the timestamp conversion carefully. 1744697460 in UTC is April 15, 2026 at 10:11 AM, while the previous heartbeat at 1744686060 was April 15 at 06:01 UTC, making it about 4 hours and 10 minutes since the last check. Looking at the cron expression `53656e40-4892-4759-a73e-a11dc01082b5`, I need to decode what schedule it represents.\n\nSince the previous heartbeat was 06:11 UTC and the current time is 10:11 UTC, that's a 4-hour gap, so the cron must be running every 4 hours. The 60-minute timeout mentioned in the instructions is just a threshold—any task exceeding that duration should be marked as Dead, but based on the cron pattern, this particular run is at the normal 4-hour interval.\n\nThe running tasks from the kanban board are all marked as \"进行中\" (in progress), so there's nothing to flag as Dead this time. Now I need to pull up the shared pool's progress database, locate the relevant table, and add the new heartbeat record."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_6qskkoxobafd_1","name":"feishu_bitable_app","arguments":{"action":"list","page_size":50}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"minimax-token-plan","model":"MiniMax-M2.7-highspeed","usage":{"in